     When the business grows, the founding team is incredibly busy. Rapid
growth puts an enormous strain on them. The business outgrows its production
facilities and management capabilities. Typically, the management crunch hits
in the third or the fourth year. That is when firms tend to outgrow their manage-
ment base with quality falling, delivery dates missed, and customers not paying
on time. As the firm enters the growth phase, the leadership team needs to ask:
what does the business need at this stage? Founding CEOs tend to depart when
their firm reaches a rapid growth phase and needs strong managerial expertise
[Boeker and Karichalil, 2002].

